-- title:
--   Degeneracy image of a cusp-regular integral function is chart-integral
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Given a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over the residue field of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'$ (rational affine geometric places at which the geometric $j$-generator takes a supersingular value), an element $s$ of $W$, and the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Further data: a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$, together with the hypothesis $hR_0$ that every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is $R_0$-integral with $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$; a prime $\ell'$ with $\ell' \ne q$, $3 \le \ell'$, $\ell' \nmid M'$; an element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity admitting a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending it to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$; and an intermediate field $K$ of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$ equal to the $k_0$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$, $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, with $K$ an $A_0$-algebra in a scalar tower over $k_0$, and a nonzero $j \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is the $\mathsf q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of the modular $j$-invariant. Finally let $gf$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ (generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series $j(\mathsf q^d)$ for $d \mid M'$), such that its image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and cusp-regular in the sense that for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ nonnegative, $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $gf$ is nonnegative as well; and assume $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $gf$ lies in $K$. Then this element, namely $g(\mathsf q^{\ell'})$, belongs to $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over the $A_0$-subalgebra generated by $j$.
--
--   This is the chart-membership step for the finite (integral-$j$) chart of the two-chart integral model of the rigid-level modular curve: it places the $\ell'$-degeneracy image $g(\mathsf q^{\ell'})$ of a cusp-regular, $R_0$-integral rational level-$M'$ function in the integral closure of $A_0[j(\mathsf q)]$ in $K$. It feeds the constructions of moduli points and Frobenius comparison on the full-level curve that cite it.
